The patient is a 40-year-old female who presents today for evaluation of back pain. The patient states that she was at a birthday party and they were all like crunched behind and hiding. When the person came in, we all jumped out, and she fell down the little stair and rammed her back into the railing of the staircase. She states that it was a surprise for her as well. She denies any pain shooting down her legs. She states that it hurts more when she is lying flat and any twisting motion for sure. The patient has a history of lumbar fusion. She denies any numbness or tingling.

