MSK: Back: There is some stiffness with rotation. No pain with leg lift or straight leg raise. No focal tenderness.

RESULTS

X-ray images of the lumbar spine obtained today show no acute abnormalities. There is no compression fracture. The patient has a lumbar fusion.

ASSESSMENT

Lumbar strain.

PLAN

I have reviewed and discussed my assessment and plan with the patient. We discussed that she has a lumbar strain. I have recommended that she continue taking Motrin 800 mg 3 times a day with food. I have also recommended that she use ice and heat, alternating on her back. I want her to continue to walk. If her symptoms worsen or do not improve over the next week, she should return for reevaluation.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up with me in 1 week if her symptoms worsen or do not improve.
