Follow-up for hypertension.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Amanda Taylor is a 72-year-old female who presents for follow-up for hypertension. She reports a history of alcohol use disorder. Her history is also significant for mild hypercholesterolemia. At her last visit on 04/16/2021, her blood pressure was 130/90. After presenting at 150/100, she was prescribed hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 mg PO daily and lisinopril 20 mg PO daily. CBC and CMP were essentially unremarkable.

The patient reports that she has been drinking 4 to 5 times a week.

She is currently taking half of the lisinopril.

She is taking the full dose of hydrochlorothiazide.

She is checking her blood pressure at home.

The patient reports that she is taking her blood pressure medications.

She has been drinking alcohol on Mondays.

She is currently taking her blood pressure medications in the morning, not in the evening.

She has received the COVID vaccine on 02/09/2021.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fever, chills, or night sweats.
• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain, dyspnea, orthopnea, or palpitations.
• Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath, cough, or sore throat.
• Musculoskeletal: Denies joint pain or swelling.
• Psychiatric: Denies anxiety, insomnia, or fatigue.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.
• Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm. No murmurs, gallop, or extra heart sounds. No peripheral edema.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

1. Alcohol use disorder.
- Medical Reasoning: The patient reports that she has been drinking 4 to 5 times a week. Her blood pressure was 150/100 when she presented at her last visit.
- Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed the potential benefits of stopping alcohol use. I explained that her blood pressure may improve completely with cessation of alcohol.
- Medical Treatment: I recommended starting Vivitrol. She will start on 05/17/2021. We reviewed side effects and risks.

2. Hypertension.
- Medical Reasoning: The patient is currently taking lisinopril 10 mg daily and hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 mg daily.
- Patient Education and Counseling: I explained that her blood pressure goal is 130-140/70-80.
- Medical Treatment: She will continue taking her current medications.

3. COVID-19.
- Medical Reasoning: She reports that she received the COVID vaccine on 02/09/2021.
- Patient Education and Counseling: I advised her to get an influenza vaccine and Shingrix.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up on 06/14/2021. }}<|eot_id|>
