Ms. Grace Ross is a pleasant 24-year-old female who presents today for full spectrum std testing. The patient states that she has symptoms of discomfort, a change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. She states that the right side of her vagina is starting to become painful. She denies any fevers or chills. She reports, that she recently learned, her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people, and she wants to be evaluated for all stds.

Ms. Ross denies any history of abnormal pap smears.

MEDICAL HISTORY

The patient reports abnormal pap smear in the past.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports she has been with her current partner for 3 years. She reports that her partner has been having multiple sexual encounters with other people for the past 3 months.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Denies fevers or chills.
Gastrointestinal: Denies abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, or constipation.
Genitourinary: Reports abnormal discharge, pain, and odor in the right side of her vagina.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Gastrointestinal: Normal bowel sounds.
Genitourinary: Examination demonstrates no external lesions. Normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge, with normal color and smell. Pelvic exam demonstrates normal cervix. Vaginal wall is normal. No cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted.

RESULTS

Std testing pending.

ASSESSMENT

• Screening for std.

PLAN

