Teresa Davis is a pleasant 70-year-old female who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of right elbow pain.

The patient reports that her pain started 4 days ago. She was working on a pottery wheel and felt a pain on the inside of her elbow. The pain radiates down her arm and along the medial aspect of her arm. She denies any direct injury. She has been taking ibuprofen but denies any relief. She reports a pain level of 7 out of 10.

The patient reports that she has a history of hypertension and is currently on 10 mg of lisinopril. She reports that her blood pressures have been in the teens to 30s. She reports that she is compliant with her medication regimen.

The patient also reports a history of diabetes. She is currently on 500 mg of metformin twice a day and reports that she is not compliant with her medication regimen. She reports that her blood sugars have been high. She reports that she likes to bake and eat sweet foods.

She reports that she enjoys doing ceramics and baking and has been making a ceramic bowl for her son's birthday. She denies any prior history of elbow injuries.

The patient reports that she is also a nature walker.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fevers.
• Musculoskeletal: Reports right elbow pain.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. No murmurs, gallop, or rub.
