ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Right elbow pain.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient's x-rays were reviewed today and they show no fracture or bony abnormality. This is consistent with a diagnosis of medial epicondylitis.
• Medical Treatment: I have prescribed a sling for the patient's right arm. I have also recommended that she apply ice to her elbow for 20 minutes three times a day. She can take 600 mg of ibuprofen every 6 hours as needed for pain and inflammation for the next week.
• Patient Education and Counseling: I advised the patient to avoid any heavy lifting or use of the affected limb for the next couple of weeks. I also advised her to continue her nature walks.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient's history of hypertension and diabetes were reviewed and discussed today. Her blood pressure was within normal limits today and her diabetes regimen was discussed. She was advised to continue her current regimen and to follow up in a couple of weeks. A referral to a diabetic counselor was also recommended.
• Patient Education and Counseling: The patient was advised to monitor and record her blood sugar levels daily. She was also advised to follow up with me in a couple of weeks.

Right hypertension.
• Medical Treatment: Continue lisinopril 10 mg daily.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient's blood pressure was within normal limits today.

Right diabetes.
• Medical Treatment: Continue metformin 500 mg twice daily.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient is not compliant with her medication regimen and her blood sugars have been high.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 2 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
