HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Jose Rodriguez is a 69-year-old male who presents for a follow-up visit. The patient had a ST elevation myocardial infarction in June 2021. He underwent stent placement in the left anterior descending artery. The patient is concerned about the amount of medications he is taking.

The patient reports that he is doing okay. He states that he is concerned that he is on a lot of medications. He notes that he is taking aspirin, Brilinta, and fish oil. He also notes that he is taking Crestor.

The patient also reports that he gets dizzy when he stands up quickly. He is on metoprolol 50 mg once a day. He wonders if this is due to the heart attack or the medication.

The patient also reports that his A1C was close to 60. He is concerned about his glucose levels. He has been watching his sweets.

The patient reports that his A1C was not where he wanted it to be, but his glucose is coming in at 1:30 fasting. He also reports that he has an affinity for chocolate chip cookies.

The patient reports that he has not had a kidney appointment in a year. He has stage 3 chronic kidney disease.

The patient has no questions at this time.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Cardiovascular: Reports dizziness when standing quickly.
• Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath.
• Musculoskeletal: Denies muscle aches.
• Psychiatric: Reports feeling down since his heart attack.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Neck: No jugular venous distention or carotid bruits.
• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally.
• Cardiovascular: Slight 3/6 systolic ejection murmur heard at the left base.
• Musculoskeletal: 1+ nonpitting edema.

RESULTS

Renal function is stable.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Jose Rodriguez is a 69-year-old male who presents for a follow-up visit. The patient had a ST elevation myocardial infarction in June 2021. He underwent stent placement in the left anterior descending artery.

Coronary artery disease.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient is stable at this time. His renal function is stable, and his blood pressure is within normal limits.
• Additional Testing: I do not think we need to proceed with a stress test at this time.
• Medical Treatment: Continue metoprolol 50 mg once daily, Crestor 40 mg once daily, and aspirin.
• Patient Education and Counseling: I advised the patient to watch his diet.

Stage 3 chronic kidney disease.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has stable renal function at this time.
• Medical Treatment: Continue to follow up with Nephrology.

Diabetes.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient has a high A1C.
• Additional Testing: Order another hemoglobin A1c.
• Medical Treatment: Continue to follow up with his primary care physician regarding his insulin regimen. I will also refer him to a dietitian for education.

