Kevin Smith is an 82-year-old male with a past medical history significant for hypertension and stage 3 chronic kidney disease, who presents for hospital follow-up after an acute on chronic CHF exacerbation.

The patient reports that he has been trying to watch his diet, but he admits to having some dietary indiscretions. He notes that he loves to eat pizza and chicken wings, and he does not always take his medications as prescribed. He was recently hospitalized for an acute on chronic CHF exacerbation. He reports that his ankles were swelling and he had shortness of breath. When he arrived at the emergency room, his blood pressure was 200/90. He denies chest pain.

The patient states that he has been feeling better since he was discharged from the hospital. He reports that he has been watching his diet and taking his medications as prescribed. He notes that he has been urinating a lot since he was in the hospital and that he has been taking a water pill through his IV. He reports that he is on different medications for his blood pressure now. He denies shortness of breath or any problems sleeping. He does report having an afternoon nap. He denies any chest pain.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain.
• Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath.
• Genitourinary: Reports increased urination.
• Musculoskeletal: Reports bilateral ankle swelling.

PHYSICAL EXAM

