• Neck: In no JVD.
• Respiratory: Lungs are clear bilaterally.
• Cardiovascular: 2/6 systolic ejection murmur, stable.
• Musculoskeletal: Trace edema in the lower extremities.

RESULTS

Echocardiogram shows a preserved ejection fraction of 55%, abnormal diastolic filling, and mild to moderate mitral regurgitation.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

1. Congestive heart failure.
• Medical Reasoning: This was caused by dietary indiscretion in uncontrolled hypertension.
• Patient Education and Counseling: I advised the patient to continue to watch his diet and to avoid salty foods. I encouraged him to continue to monitor his blood pressure at home.
